omparisons I want to stick to the  smaller sized iPad Pro and the iPad Air  because it's the most similar to the  current budget iPad now getting started  apple pencil support came to the 9.7  inch iPad Pro and early 2016 and it only  came to the 6th gen budget iPad in early  2018. so that took about two years to  make its way down moving on in early  2019 the iPad Air 3 received the a12  chip which only made its way down to the  budget iPad 8 in late 2020 which is  about a one and a half year difference  the iPad Air 3 was also the first Air  Model to come come with 64 gigs of Base  storage and it wasn't until late 2021  when the current budget iPad 9 started  coming with 64 gigs which is a two and a  half year difference on top of that the  air 3 also received the true tone  display which didn't come to the budget  iPad until this current iPad 9 which is  also a two and a half year difference so  if we take all of that and average it  out it seems like a lot of the  hand-me-downs take around two to two and  a half years to make their way down to  the budget iPad now before I apply that  to the timeline of when each iPad  received a full flat sided redesign I  want to bust out the recent leaks and  rumors we got concerning the budget iPad  10 and see if those timelines match up  first of all we got a leak from the king  of Apple display leaks Ross young who  has been banging on with exact display  detail leaks in the past including the  14 and 16 inch MacBook Pro displays the  8.3 inch had mini 6 display and even the  13.6 inch M2 MacBook Air and recently he  claimed that the new iPad is going to be  getting a 10.5 inch display while the  iPad Air will remain at 10.9 which  totally makes sense because Apple wants  the more expensive iPads to have larger  displays now if that 10.5 inch display  size sounds familiar it should because  that's precisely the display size of the  iPad Air 3 and 2019 and not only that  but the entire chassis and the 10.5 inch  display on 